# Android / Gradle
#
# The Gradle wrapper JAR is intentionally NOT ignored — see the note at the
# bottom of this file.

## Build output
build/
app/build/
.gradle/
captures/
out/
release/

## Local SDK location. Machine-specific, never committed; CI resolves the SDK
## from ANDROID_HOME instead.
local.properties

## Packaged apps
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.dex

## Signing material. Nothing in this repository is signed with a real key, and
## nothing ever should be — the release job produces an unsigned APK on purpose.
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties

## Android Studio / IntelliJ
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.navigation/
.cxx/

## Kotlin
.kotlin/

## Java
*.class
*.log
hs_err_pid*

## Lint and test output
lint-results*.html
lint-results*.xml
app/lint-baseline.xml

## Emulator and adb noise
*.hprof
screenshots/

## OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
#
# Committing the wrapper jar is the Gradle-recommended practice and is what
# makes `./gradlew` work on a fresh clone. It is a binary, so it cannot be
# generated by hand — run `gradle wrapper` once with a system Gradle and commit
# the result.
#
# CI does not depend on it: the workflow installs Gradle through
# gradle/actions/setup-gradle and calls `gradle` directly, so the pipeline is
# green with or without the jar present.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
